id: pmc-hox8
title: "Suppressed pending release can relocate or drop an item (Greptile issue 2, PR #174)"
description: Suppressing a pending release window can silently relocate or drop an item declaring the suppressed version — Greptile issue 2 on PR #174. Routing is now constrained to the suppressed release only.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: bug,greptile,pr-174
created_at: "2026-08-31T11:19:54.090Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-01T06:32:50.778Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-31T11:24:28.443Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-31T11:24:28.443Z"
author: pi-agent
resolution: Constrained assignItemsToReleaseWindows to route only a declaration naming the suppressed pending release to Unreleased; every other unmatched declaration keeps its timestamp placement and timestamp attribution classification.
expected_result: Only a declaration naming the suppressed pending release routes to Unreleased; other unmatched declarations keep their timestamp placement. The suppressed item survives section narrowing.
actual_result: "Four tests pass: suppressed declarations do not relocate into an older real release; suppressed declarations do not drop under section narrowing; a stale or misspelled declaration keeps its timestamp placement and attribution; a suppressed declaration keeps timestamp placement when no Unreleased window exists. Reverting the constrained routing to unconditional orphan routing turns the stale-declaration test red (items pulled out of their tagged release)."
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-31T11:23:34.180Z",pi-agent,"Fixed: assignItemsToReleaseWindows now routes items whose declared release matches no window to the Unreleased section, preventing relocation to older releases and omission by section narrowing. Three revert-proof tests: relocated-to-older-release, omitted-by-narrowing (with --since-version), and correct Unreleased placement."
  "2026-09-01T06:32:50.778Z",claude,"Execution evidence for the recorded outcome (addressing CodeRabbit's request that outcomes carry evidence, not intent). Each of the four recorded test commands was executed against this branch on 2026-09-01 and each matched exactly one real test title and passed. Verified with the run counts, not the exit code, because --test-name-pattern is a regex and a pattern that matches nothing still exits 0: 'suppressed pending release does not relocate' tests=1 pass=1 fail=0; 'suppressed pending release does not drop' tests=1 pass=1 fail=0; 'a stale or misspelled release declaration keeps its timestamp placement and attribution' tests=1 pass=1 fail=0; 'a suppressed declaration keeps timestamp placement when no Unreleased window exists' tests=1 pass=1 fail=0."
