  "PM_PATH=/tmp/pmc-hox8 PM_GLOBAL_PATH=/tmp/pmc-hox8-g node --test --test-name-pattern \"a suppressed declaration keeps timestamp placement when no Unreleased window exists\" test/generator.test.ts",test/generator.test.ts,project,"a suppressed declaration keeps timestamp placement when no Unreleased window exists (includeUnreleased:false opt-out preserved)"
close_reason: Fixed and verified
body: "## Reasoning (causal path, unexecuted analysis)\n\nGreptile review on PR #174 (confidence 3/5): when tagged history contains an item declaring the suppressed placeholder version, with a completion time at or before the newest real tag, removing the pending window leaves no matching release identity. The timestamp fallback then renders that item under an older real release, and section narrowing can drop it entirely. So suppressing a phantom release can silently attribute work to a real past release or lose it.\n\n## Fix applied (constrained)\n\nassignItemsToReleaseWindows routes ONLY a declaration naming the suppressed pending release (suppressedPendingRelease, the pending version removed by pendingRelease: false) to the Unreleased window, without consulting a timestamp. Every other unmatched declaration — stale, misspelled, or naming a tag the window list excludes — keeps its historical timestamp-based placement and classification, so ordinary --all-release-tags runs are unaffected (Greptile's over-correction finding). When no Unreleased window exists (includeUnreleased: false) the suppressed declaration falls through to timestamp placement, preserving the caller's explicit opt-out. Attribution provenance (isPlacedByReleaseDeclaration) recognises the suppressed-key routing as a release pin so the release_pinned bucket does not leak."
